  "task": "Thoroughly explore the Unity project at D:\\unity\\project\\LightTest2d to understand its full architecture. I need to understand:\n\n1. Read ALL C# scripts under Assets/Scripts/ (including subdirectories: Buff, Bullet, Currency, Enemy, Interface, Item, Map, Player, Skill, SystemUI, and root files like PlayerController2D.cs, CameraFollow2D.cs, DamagePopup.cs)\n\n2. List all prefabs under Assets/Prefabs/ (Boss, Enemy, Items, Projectiles, Rooms, UI, Player.prefab) - what components do they have?\n\n3. List all resources under Assets/Resources/ (Enemy, Map, Skills, TestAssets)\n\n4. List all textures/assets under Assets/Textures/ and Assets/Textures/Map/\n\n5. Check Assets/Settings/ for URP renderer and pipeline assets\n\n6. Check the existing SampleScene hierarchy\n\nReport back:\n- Complete class hierarchy and inheritance for all scripts\n- What components each prefab uses (SpriteRenderer, Rigidbody2D, colliders, custom scripts, etc.)\n- What the Map system looks like (Tilemap? Sprite-based? Room system?)\n- How the Player works (movement, health, skills, etc.)\n- What the Enemy system looks like\n- What the Bullet/Projectile system looks like\n- What the Skill system looks like\n- What the Buff system looks like\n- What the Item system looks like\n- What the UI system looks like\n- What the Currency system looks like\n- What the DamagePopup system looks like\n- What materials and textures are used\n- What the URP 2D renderer settings are (especially light blend styles, shadow settings)\n\nBe very thorough - read every script file completely."
}
